 "_": "Rail plate — the front of the rotating group. A Ø100 disc: the strip across its middle carries the MGN9 rail on its OUTER face, tapped M3 at the rail’s own 20 mm pitch, and the screw’s Ø6.2 journal runs in a blind bore at its centre, closed by the rail itself. Either side of the strip a long slot lets a coupling link pass through, over and under the rail. Two M8 tapped holes at x ±24 take the pillars, drawn at the tap drill and blind because the rail closes them off. Nothing bolts to a case any more: the case does not turn and this does. One extrude along -Y.",
